+## Compact head refresh, 2026-09-12
+
+The prior selected small source was retained as rejected silhouette evidence after review at the native 30x12 map-counter footprint. These are the refresh prompts for the compact transparent head and upper-shoulder pair.
+
+### Small frame 0, compact normal
+
+Create an original compact two-dimensional map-counter silhouette for a demonic zombie infantry unit on a genuinely transparent background. Show a broad horned skull, a narrow powerful neck, bold bat-wing edge silhouettes rising behind the shoulders, and pointed claw-like shoulder edges designed to survive a 30 by 12 pixel frame. Preserve the demonic identity from the existing neutral model guidance: horned head, bat-like wing membranes, and clawed shoulder edges. Use the restrained pale vanilla map-counter value range, crisp edges, and no scenery. Keep the subject centered with transparent padding. Do not include text, symbols, border, UI frame, terrain, checkerboard, opaque background, glow, or photorealistic rendering.
+
+### Small frame 1, compact pale schematic
+
+Create an original compact two-dimensional pale schematic map-counter state for a demonic zombie infantry unit on a genuinely transparent background. Depict only a centered horned skull and upper-shoulder emblem with a narrow neck, two swept horns, and bold bat-wing edge silhouettes behind the shoulders. Use pale grey to near-white sparse schematic marks with darker charcoal internal separations and open transparent gaps, designed to survive a 30 by 12 pixel frame. Keep the emblem bold and readable against a dark map UI backing. Do not include text, symbols, border, UI frame, terrain, checkerboard, opaque background, glow, colour wash, or photorealistic rendering.
+
+Anatomy guidance for this refresh remained the existing `blender/previews/resume_demonic_neutral_front.png` and `blender/previews/resume_demonic_neutral_right.png`; those references supplied no runtime pixels.
