+## Compact head-counter refresh, 2026-09-12
+
+Parent review found that the prior full-body small silhouette did not retain enough head and upper-shoulder identity at the native 30x12 footprint. The prior selected small source frames, processed frames, sheet, DDS, round-trip, and comparison previews are preserved under `source/candidates/rejected_small_frame*_silhouette_legibility.png`, `source/rejected_silhouette_imagegen_small_frame*.png`, and `previews/rejected_small_silhouette_legibility*` and are excluded from the refreshed production evidence.
+
+The refreshed small frame 0 is an original compact transparent head and upper-shoulder emblem with a broad helmet-like skull, thick snarling jaw, massive neck, and broad shoulders. The refreshed small frame 1 is its original pale sparse schematic companion with the same heavy jaw and neck identity.
+
+The native origins are recorded in `source/native_imagegen_origins.md` and the exact prompts in `prompts/generation_prompts.md`. Explicit compact copies are retained as `source/candidates/candidate_small_frame0_compact.png`, `source/candidates/candidate_small_frame1_compact.png`, `source/imagegen_small_frame0_compact.png`, and `source/imagegen_small_frame1_compact.png`; the standard candidate and selected source names now point to the same new native outputs for processing.
+
+The installed pale map-counter frame 0 palette and alpha policy remain unchanged. The refreshed normal frame has 79 opaque and 40 partial pixels with opaque luma 94/192/236 minimum/median/maximum, and the frame remains transparent outside the emblem with no painted backing or halo.
+
+The refreshed small frame is compared with the installed vanilla frame on the same dark backing in `previews/small_normal_vs_vanilla_review.png`. The compact-head evidence remains pending parent visual acceptance.
+
+The large processed sheet remains byte-fixed at `8a9569526fc18f4c3933a2c131a15010e8e0ffb06bd81040a1d9ec59517e93c4`, and its evidence DDS remains byte-fixed at `556371d5321dd354b2d66edbe3e58ee92cbde85539cb0ff30975e1b40b9b464b`. Parent-owned runtime bytes remain untouched.
