+## Compact head-counter refresh, 2026-09-12
+
+Parent review found that the prior full-body small silhouette did not retain enough head and upper-shoulder identity at the native 30x12 footprint. The prior selected small source frames, processed frames, sheet, DDS, round-trip, and comparison previews are preserved under `source/candidates/rejected_small_frame*_silhouette_legibility.png`, `source/rejected_silhouette_imagegen_small_frame*.png`, and `previews/rejected_small_silhouette_legibility*` and are excluded from the refreshed production evidence.
+
+The refreshed small frame 0 is an original compact transparent head and upper-shoulder emblem with a broad skull, bulbous one-sided parasitic growth, and one curled tendril beside the skull. The refreshed small frame 1 is its original pale sparse schematic companion with the same parasite and tendril identity.
+
+The native origins are recorded in `source/native_imagegen_origins.md` and the exact prompts in `prompts/generation_prompts.md`. Explicit compact copies are retained as `source/candidates/candidate_small_frame0_compact.png`, `source/candidates/candidate_small_frame1_compact.png`, `source/imagegen_small_frame0_compact.png`, and `source/imagegen_small_frame1_compact.png`; the standard candidate and selected source names now point to the same new native outputs for processing.
+
+The installed pale map-counter frame 0 palette and alpha policy remain unchanged. The refreshed normal frame has 94 opaque and 37 partial pixels with opaque luma 94/190/236 minimum/median/maximum, and the frame remains transparent outside the emblem with no painted backing or halo.
+
+The refreshed small sheet and DDS are compared with the installed vanilla frame on the same dark backing in `previews/small_normal_vs_vanilla_review.png`, and all four refreshed units are shown together in `previews/small_compact_four_unit_vs_vanilla_review.png`. The global review is stored in this package because it is bounded visual evidence only; it does not add runtime wiring.
+
+The large processed sheet remains byte-fixed at `b72f4f3a49454a35e8cad72f84444fbc7bf2c5d29017585cb151282b6dd304e4`, and its evidence DDS remains byte-fixed at `c5f830fd94f874e31343071e3d3b905f06939e0e2fdd86664fe4a5829c52f07c`. Parent-owned runtime bytes remain untouched.
