+12,Africa Is One,"An African government has started pulling the continent together with aid, guarantees, liberation deals, and a common Charter. Other countries can join, bargain, walk away, or build a rival camp. If the project keeps its promises, regional congresses and constitutional settlements can turn the idea into roads, armies, laws, and a fierce argument over who carries the cost.
+
+After Evolution I, the African unifier must survive the consolidation of its institutions before its leaders proclaim the Gods of Africa layer. Every major and player-controlled country receives an independent Wrath of the Gods relationship. The unifier issues recurring, capacity-checked demands tied to real continental needs, with a frozen amount, deadline, and response path shown in the Gods of Africa category. Demand families include land equipment, support equipment, fuel, manpower, industrial repair support, emergency relief, transport reserves, aircraft reserves, recognition, return of an African core state, termination of recorded support for an African enemy, and a strategic-resource concession paid through the real give_resource_rights steel lane. Participants can fulfil, partially pay, request an extension, submit a frozen substitute for acceptance, refuse, or permanently defy. The repaired response paths cover substitutes, timeouts, wartime responses, pardons, offender escalation, and lifecycle counters. Judgment reach gates offender escalation; sanctions add bounded punishment memory; sanctuary and security can turn protection into a real guarantee or military-access compact. Gods of Africa Strength caps punishment. Broader transport, intelligence, reconstruction, disaster, migration, and trade protection families remain open. When Africa secures the continent, ordinary demands end and each surviving participant receives one final settlement outcome.
+
+Full probability, live GUI, and save validation remain open.","The Charter League has kept its first promise and can finally look beyond one corridor. Regional congresses, negotiated settlements, restoration claims, and rival blocs will decide whether its protection grows into lasting cooperation.
+
+The Gods of Africa path opens after Evolution I and the consolidation milestone. The first relationship notices establish independent Wrath for major and player-controlled countries. Capacity-checked demands can request land equipment, support equipment, fuel, manpower, industrial repair support, emergency relief, transport reserves, or aircraft reserves, and the repaired relationship paths record substitutes, timeouts, and wartime responses.","The League is settling into daily life. Shared railways, emergency forces, membership law, and resource bargains tie distant courts together, and every new connection brings another bill or obligation.
+
+As the continental machinery grows, Gods of Africa demands can scale through land equipment, aircraft, and industrial repair support. Each demand freezes one amount, deadline, and response path, and each participant can have only one active demand. Evolution II opens advanced security integration, core recognition, federalisation, resource review, continental industry, citizenship, and emergency leadership actions. As their conditions and political-power capacity become available, Gods of Africa can add recognition, return of an African core state, termination of recorded support for an African enemy, and a strategic-resource concession through the real give_resource_rights steel lane. Real protection packages are paid from African capacity for reliable partners. Support-equipment and aircraft priority lanes, and elephant logistics, remain bounded by their own capability and target gates. The elephant formation uses sprite = elephantry, reusing the normal vanilla Elephantry model and animation family; no custom elephant entity, model, or animation route is promoted. Punishment can damage infrastructure, but stronger responses still require both capability and cause under the current Strength ceiling.","Africa's settlement has become a question every great power must answer. Foreign bases, sanctions, continent-wide mobilization, strange new actors, and rival projects are now part of the same struggle.
+
+At world-pole scale, permanent defiance ends ordinary demands and closes the normal friendship route. Punishment, protection duties, retaliation, and costly reconciliation remain possible, while judgment reach gates offender escalation and sanctions preserve bounded punishment memory. Sanctuary and security can turn protection into a real guarantee or military-access compact. Stronger punishment remains bounded by Gods of Africa Strength and the participant's Wrath, as the final campaign records the conduct that will shape settlement. Broader transport, intelligence, reconstruction, disaster, migration, and trade protection families remain open. The installed Gods decision probability pool remains incomplete; no normalized probability comparison, live GUI acceptance, or save validation is claimed.",,,"The World: Unanimous Continental Union
+
+The African host completed the constitutional agreement for a unanimous continental union and leads The World resolution. Continental governments now follow the settlement's public terms.
+
+The World: Last Standing Resolution
+
+The African host survived as the last continental government and leads The World resolution. Its final settlement defines the new order.
+
+The World: Continental Campaign
+
+The African host won the final continental campaign and leads the new world order. The settlement binds the continent's rival governments under its terms.
+
+ONE WORLD REMAINS
+
+The last continental rivalries have ended. The African host reached The World through a final protocol founded on consent and a public settlement. Its constitution, surviving obligations, and treatment of defeated rivals now define the final order.
+
+Gods of Africa relationship history shapes invitations, conditions, privileges, and opposition throughout the World Is One campaign.",Minor Fire-Once,4,6,Needs Testing
