+If the plague is allowed to settle in, the rats may become something more dangerous than carriers. Whole warrens can learn to fight, govern, and follow a king of their own.","The plague has learned to thrive in crowded and poorly protected places. Deaths rise faster, and every untreated corridor helps the next wave spread.","Ports and long-distance transport carry the plague beyond its mainland cradle. Docks, troop convoys, refugees, and wartime shipping can open a second front across the sea.",Collapsed plague basins have joined one Rat Nation. Its broods seize infected ground and build armies without human soldiers or ordinary equipment.,"A royal basin has learned to obey one sentient ruler. The Rat King gathers memory, hunger, and authority as the surviving broods decide whether to kneel.","The Rat King's dominion has grown beyond the warrens. Capitals fall silent, refuges are overrun, and the last continental cordons begin to break.","The Rat King rules from the Royal Basin, where the plague's surviving broods gather under one crown. Fallen capitals and overrun refuges feed a kingdom that carries its warrens, human servants, and royal hunger across the world.",Minor Fire-Once,1,13,Needs Testing
+21,Random Civil War,"A country's chain of command has split between rival political and military authorities. Capitals, supply routes, public legitimacy, and the terms offered to each front will shape the conflict.
+
+Settlement
+
+The sides have accepted terms based on recognition, autonomy, coalition, partition, or disarmament. The peace will last only if every signatory meets its obligations.
+
+Reconstruction
+
+The fighting has ended. Repaired railways, restored civil administration, demobilization, and fulfilled peace terms will determine whether the settlement lasts.","Additional commands and regional movements have entered the first war. Several rival authorities are now competing for capitals, supply routes, and terms of peace.","Arms routes, sponsors, and displaced administrations are carrying the crisis across borders. Civilian relief and armed support now demand separate choices.","Countries are moving from stability into exposure, fracture, and open crisis as divided commands and regional movements test weakened governments. Victory, reform, and negotiated terms can still restore public authority.",,,,Minor Repeatable,1,1,Needs Testing
+22,Spain Antisemitism,"A violent antisemitic faction emerges during the Spanish Civil War, seeks an alliance with Nazi Germany, and threatens Jewish communities across Europe.",,,,,,,Minor Fire-Once,1,18,To Be Reworked
+23,SOV Nuclear Bombs,"The Soviet atomic arsenal opens a guarded program of production, testing, coercion, command, custody, and possible exchange. Every device remains tied to a physical depot, an accountable authority, trained delivery crews, and a release order; a Soviet collapse can scatter custody without granting immediate launch capability.","The breakthrough becomes a wider nuclear program, expanding the event-owned stockpile and reactor network while keeping control, readiness, and accounting in tension.","Coercive doctrine opens selected demands against valid minor powers and Soviet breakaways, with delivery evidence, target behavior, and settlement terms shaping the result.","A valid nuclear-major rival opens retaliation and the first nonterminal exchange warning, but the world-state gate must exist before multi-major conflict can begin.","The widest Soviet response profile becomes available, while Soviet AI first use remains rare and requires severe strategic losses, an operational nuclear major target, a viable route, intact command, and no verified stand-down.",,,Minor Fire-Once,2,,Playable
+24,Video Game in Sweden,"Sweden created an advanced campaign simulation from relay cabinets, projected maps, and printed scenario sheets. The military can use it for training and analysis. If its circulation widens, its categories may pass from staff officers into schoolrooms, factory schedules, and diplomatic files, where a tidy forecast can become an order.","The Staff College Takes the Board
+
+Swedish officers have made the cabinet part of professional culture, with rankings, repeated scenarios, and a growing dispute over what the tables truly measure.","The Nation Takes Its Turn
+
+Clubs, schools, newspapers, and workplaces have turned the Swedish cabinet into a public institution. Evening leagues alter factory shifts, teachers use its campaigns to discuss geography, and political organisers cite its simplified alignments in municipal halls.","When the Board Directs the Cabinet
+
+Senior offices are applying the cabinet's categories to transport, weather, production, diplomacy, and real operations.",,,,Minor Fire-Once,1,,Needs Testing
