+26,Black Friday,"A Friday clearance sale draws crowds into shops across the world. Quartermasters, intelligence officers, and ministry clerks join the rush, bringing government orders to counters already piled with civilian purchases.","If this evolution is enabled and chaos is at least [?constant:black_friday_event.evolution_chaos|0] when the sale begins, eligible purchases receive [?constant:black_friday_event.evolution_discount_percent|0]% off. That rate lasts until the next daily tick, even if chaos falls.",,,,,,Minor Fire-Once,1,,Needs Testing
+27,Doctrine Research,Military academies across the world periodically receive a shared curriculum. Each curriculum grants one choice at first and as many as five in later stages. A choice can establish a Grand Doctrine or advance one eligible subdoctrine by one mastery step.,Each participating country receives two doctrine choices. A choice can establish one eligible Grand Doctrine or advance one eligible subdoctrine by one mastery step.,Each participating country receives three doctrine choices. These choices can deepen one branch or develop several eligible tracks.,Each participating country receives four doctrine choices. Countries with established Grand Doctrines can divide those choices among several eligible tracks.,Each participating country receives five doctrine choices. A country can complete one branch or spread its mastery across several eligible tracks.,,,Minor Repeatable,1,9,Needs Testing
+28,Asteroid Incoming,"A global, fire-once asteroid episode records a locked impact coordinate, its cross-border footprint, actual deaths and destruction, atmospheric dust, fragment sites, recovery decisions, and control of extraordinary mineral sites. The opening choice presents three distinct country and state coordinates plus a genuine near miss; a confirmed impact locks the coordinate for two days and destroys the centre state while three land rings are damaged across borders, leaving a permanent crater. A miss records no physical consequence.","Global Fragmentation — Chaos Tier, 600 Chaos, Stage 1: The chosen main body still strikes, while separated fragments hit several valid states worldwide with smaller damage rings and additional dust.","Extraordinary Minerals — Totalen Chaos, 800 Chaos, Stage 1, requires Global Fragmentation: Main and fragment crater control grants transferable land-division armour bonuses, with plus 100 percent from the main crater and plus 20 percent per fragment site.",,,,,Major,1,,Needs Testing
+29,Riches Found,"A random country receives a major political windfall when a valuable deposit is found in one eligible state. The discovery can transform an isolated district into a crowded mining settlement, and the mine remains tied to that state, with persistent income and industrial value following whoever controls it. Its controller must regulate claims, build transport and housing, settle the revenue, manage concessions and security, resist foreign capture, and keep extraction from outrunning public authority as workers, companies, guards, officials, criminals, and foreign interests struggle over access and control. When no valid country and state pair exists, Event Details shows N/A.","The mine's wealth begins capturing the state, government, companies, security services, and public spending. Concession holders buy protection, officials trade access, and public revenue disappears before it reaches the treasury. Choose public revenue, national control, private domination, concession dependence, or tolerated corruption; harder extraction improves the mine while worsening dependence and capture.","Gold Disease spreads an obsessive hunger for the mine's gold among workers, officials, guards, soldiers, and administrators. Theft, hoarding, barricaded workings, and violent disputes threaten the district; choose revenue sharing, workforce replacement, military intervention, quarantine, temporary closure, or sealing deeper sections. Continued extraction raises output while driving the crisis higher.","Deep excavation opens sealed chambers occupied by a corrupting underground force. Disappearances, altered workers, impossible accidents, mass violence, military breakdown, and severe state pressure follow as armed figures demand payment in labor, metal, and obedience. Choose to seal the depths, evacuate, seek religious or occult assistance, exploit the mine under control, purge the threat, or make an agreement.",,,,Minor Repeatable,1,"7, 15",Needs Testing
+30,Time Traveler,"A time traveler known as “Time Traveler” advises a country and warns certain governments against wars that history says they will lose. A later route can bring Napoleon back, followed by a robot invasion from the future.",Time Traveler: a historical warning system guides governments away from wars that history says they will lose.,,,"Napoleon returns (Pretzel Logic), World End scenario: army of robots from the future invade, basically like in the movie Terminator.",,,Major,1,,To Be Reworked
+31,Random Terror,"Violence erupts in a random country, damaging buildings and killing civilians.",,,,,,,Minor Repeatable,1,16,To Be Reworked
+32,Missiles,"Missile programmes have spread across the world. Countries can build and harden launch sites, stock operational missiles, improve guidance, and secure the officers and codes that control them. Heavier arsenals, guidance failures, special warheads, rogue commands, and automatic retaliation can transform the crisis.","Growing reserves and larger launch sites can support massed salvos. Saturation attacks can overwhelm defences, but they consume many missiles and strain readiness and command control.","Faulty guidance can send missiles away from their intended targets. Drift, false warnings, interception, and damage to launch sites force commanders to investigate failures and contain their consequences.","Countries that already possess chemical, biological, nuclear, or thermonuclear weapons can adapt them for missile delivery. Each launch still requires an authorised warhead held in secure custody.","A compromised launch site can break from lawful authority while its crews still hold missiles and warheads. The government must regain control through new codes, isolation, negotiation, loyal forces, or the destruction of the site.","Governments can delegate retaliation to officers or automatic warning systems. A disputed alert may be verified, delayed, or stopped by severing the network before missiles leave their sites.",,Minor Repeatable,1,,Needs Testing
+33,Acid Rain,"A lethal atmospheric system moves through a frozen registry of valid states, touching each state exactly once while prepared countries spend resources to limit deaths, damage, contamination, and supply loss before the ordinary cloud dissipates.","Severe Storm Cells: localized high-intensity cells add stronger human, infrastructure, supply, and military pressure while the regional system continues moving.","Multiple Weather Fronts: two independent fronts can operate at once, with a conditional third front, separate warnings, timers, intensity, and severe cells.","Global Acid Rain: simultaneous worldwide exposure closes the regional phase, applies the same exact population-loss contract everywhere, and retains a guaranteed dissipation path.",,,,Major,2,5,To Be Reworked
+34,Industrial Boom,"The expansion records its overheating, reserves, projects, supplier ties, regions, and reach. A hard landing turns those strengths and liabilities into the opening conditions of Great Depression 2.0.",,,,,,,Minor Repeatable,1,7,To Be Reworked
+35,Great Depression 2.0,"Great Depression 2.0 follows a national economy from panic and contraction through depression, stabilization, and recovery. Depression Severity measures the public crisis while distressed industrial centers, foreign exposure, social peace, and the government's recovery doctrine shape the road out.","Trade, credit, and supplier ties carry the panic across borders. Exposed partners can send aid, redirect supply, protect domestic finance, or withdraw before foreign strain becomes a depression of its own.","Organized movements turn prolonged hardship into strikes, emergency mandates, and regional demands. Political collapse or armed conflict follows only when the government loses control of the actors and institutions that could still contain them.","A worldwide contraction links national recoveries through failing demand, vulnerable suppliers, and scarce credit. Countries can protect themselves, support exposed partners, or assemble an international reconstruction effort strong enough to restore trade.",,,,Minor Repeatable,1,10,Needs Testing
