@@ -123,7 +123,7 @@ chaosx.nr16.6.xenobiological_synthesis.d: "The first reproducible prototype of [
 chaosx.nr16.6.biological_weapons.d: "The first reproducible prototype of [This.GetBrilliantScientistBreakthroughProjectName] has passed its sealed validation. The result is a weapon and a public-health threat in the same ledger, so the question of disclosure is inseparable from the question of whether anyone can contain it. [This.GetBrilliantScientistHostFlavorClause] [This.GetBrilliantScientistCountryFlavorClause]"
 chaosx.nr16.6.alien_arms.d: "The first reproducible prototype of [This.GetBrilliantScientistBreakthroughProjectName] has answered the Directorate's interface protocol without destroying its operators. The proof is incomplete, but it is enough to make foreign intelligence services treat the laboratory as a strategic frontier. [This.GetBrilliantScientistHostFlavorClause] [This.GetBrilliantScientistCountryFlavorClause]"
 chaosx.nr16.6.temporal.d: "The first reproducible prototype of [This.GetBrilliantScientistBreakthroughProjectName] has returned a consistent record from a test that should have produced incompatible histories. The archive now contains evidence that time can be handled as a technical problem, and a debt that cannot be erased by filing it away. [This.GetBrilliantScientistHostFlavorClause] [This.GetBrilliantScientistCountryFlavorClause]"
-chaosx.nr16.6.singularity.d: "The first reproducible prototype of [This.GetBrilliantScientistBreakthroughProjectName] has linked its first components without entering the terminal state. The Directorate has proved that the architecture can grow, which makes every later approval a decision about a future the government may no longer be able to close. [This.GetBrilliantScientistHostFlavorClause] [This.GetBrilliantScientistCountryFlavorClause]"
+chaosx.nr16.6.singularity.d: "The first reproducible prototype of [This.GetBrilliantScientistBreakthroughProjectName] has linked its first components without arming or activating the device. The Directorate has proved that the architecture can grow, which makes every later approval a decision about a future the government may no longer be able to close. [This.GetBrilliantScientistHostFlavorClause] [This.GetBrilliantScientistCountryFlavorClause]"
 chaosx.nr16.6.default.d: "The first reproducible prototype has survived the test bench and produced a result that staff outside Kruger's private notation can inspect. The Directorate has produced evidence that the government must decide how much of it should enter public institutions. [This.GetBrilliantScientistHostFlavorClause] [This.GetBrilliantScientistCountryFlavorClause]"
 chaosx.nr16.6.a: "Publish the validated result."
 chaosx.nr16.6.b: "Seal it in the strategic ledger."
