 ﻿l_english:
-chaosx.nr23.1.t: "Soviet Nuclear Bombs"
+chaosx.nr23.1.t: "SOV Nuclear Bombs"
 
-chaosx.nr23.2.t: "Nuclear Bombs"
-chaosx.nr23.2.d: "Our scientists have completed one hundred nuclear weapons. The arsenal gives the Soviet Union a new power over its enemies and places every capital within reach."
-chaosx.nr23.2.a: "The arsenal is ready."
+chaosx.nr23.2.t: "The Arsenal Opens"
+chaosx.nr23.2.d: "The Soviet research directorate has completed the first dedicated atomic arsenal. A new reserve enters the ledger without replacing any weapon already held by the Union. Reactors, guarded depots, delivery crews, and command procedures will decide whether this power remains a secret reserve or becomes an instrument of war."
+chaosx.nr23.2.party: "Place the arsenal under Party custody"
+chaosx.nr23.2.military: "Place the arsenal under military custody"
+chaosx.nr23.2.scientific_safety: "Require a scientific safety veto"
+chaosx.nr23.2.dispersed_commands: "Disperse custody among regional commands"
 
-chaosx.news.23.t: "Soviet Might"
-chaosx.news.23.d: "The Soviet Union has announced the production of one hundred nuclear weapons. Governments are revising their defenses as the arsenal places every major city under the shadow of nuclear attack."
-chaosx.news.23.a: "The scale is alarming."
+chaosx.nr23.100.t: "The Nuclear Command Board"
+chaosx.nr23.100.d: "The command board has assigned custody, guarded each depot, and opened a ledger for every device. Its officers will record tests, production, foreign pressure, custody disputes, and every weapon placed under an authorization order."
+chaosx.nr23.100.a: "Keep the record exact."
+chaosx.nr23.101.t: "Atomic Test Report"
+chaosx.nr23.101.d: "The proof-test report has reached the command board. Instruments, evacuation plans, and the selected test site determine whether the demonstration confirms a working weapon, exposes a failure, or becomes an accident."
+chaosx.nr23.101.a: "Read the report."
+chaosx.nr23.102.t: "A Test Has Gone Wrong"
+chaosx.nr23.102.d: "The latest atomic test has ended badly. The device remains accounted for, but the failure has damaged confidence in the arsenal and exposed weaknesses in the command chain."
+chaosx.nr23.102.a: "Secure the surviving record."
+chaosx.nr23.106.t: "The Nuclear Race Widens"
+chaosx.nr23.106.d: "Foreign bomber patrols, reactor compounds, and military observers treat the Soviet arsenal as a strategic fact. Moscow is expanding fissile production and tightening command procedures while every weapon remains in the central ledger."
+chaosx.nr23.106.a: "Expand the program under control."
+chaosx.nr23.110.t: "The Breakaway Custody Board"
+chaosx.nr23.110.d: "A registered depot has crossed a Soviet political fracture. Physical custody does not provide technical access, a command authority, or an integrated delivery force. The breakaway holds the devices without inheriting the means to use them."
+chaosx.nr23.110.a: "Open the custody review."
+chaosx.nr23.120.t: "The Ultimatum Reaches the Capital"
+chaosx.nr23.120.d: "[ROOT.GetName] has received the Soviet demand: [GetSovietNuclearBombsDemandName]. Its government can accept the terms, offer a limited settlement, delay while seeking foreign backing, or refuse. The reply will shape Soviet credibility and the next command decision without starting a war by itself."
+chaosx.nr23.120.a: "Accept the Soviet terms."
+chaosx.nr23.120.b: "Accept a partial settlement."
+chaosx.nr23.120.c: "Delay the answer."
+chaosx.nr23.120.refuse: "Refuse the demand."
+chaosx.nr23.120.e: "Expose the channel."
+chaosx.nr23.120.f: "Seek foreign support."
+chaosx.nr23.140.t: "Authorization Record"
+chaosx.nr23.140.d: "A release order has reached the authorization board. Technical certification, target validity, delivery readiness, command integrity, and the reserved device must all be verified before the strike can proceed."
+chaosx.nr23.140.a: "Confirm the order."
+chaosx.nr23.150.t: "The Exchange Has Begun"
+chaosx.nr23.150.d: "A confirmed nuclear detonation has been answered by another major power. Communications are failing, retaliation windows are opening, and the first exchange between nuclear powers has begun. Fallout is spreading from each blast as commanders decide whether the next orders will widen the war."
+chaosx.nr23.150.a: "Keep the line open."
+chaosx.nr23.160.t: "Moratorium Verification"
+chaosx.nr23.160.d: "The Soviet Union has entered an atomic moratorium. Release orders are suspended, active strike and retaliation planning has ended, and the ledger must remain reconciled while the command board verifies that no device is left outside custody."
+chaosx.nr23.160.a: "Verify the moratorium."
+chaosx.nr23.161.t: "Reciprocal Stand-Down Review"
+chaosx.nr23.161.d: "The hotline agreement has reached its verification date. The command board must confirm that both nuclear powers accepted the same verification number, suspended new release orders, and kept their command authorities intact throughout the pause."
+chaosx.nr23.161.a: "Review the agreement."
+chaosx.nr23.162.t: "Settlement Review"
+chaosx.nr23.162.d: "The response to [GetSovietNuclearBombsDemandName] has reached its verification date. The settlement with [sov_nuclear_bombs_coercion_target.GetName] remains valid only if that government is independent, has not capitulated, and still enforces the agreed terms."
+chaosx.nr23.162.a: "Review the settlement."
+chaosx.nr23.163.t: "A Reciprocal Stand-Down Offer"
+chaosx.nr23.163.d: "Moscow has suspended its release orders and asks us to do the same under verification number [?sov_nuclear_bombs_standdown_offer_nonce|0]. Acceptance binds this government to the pause. Refusal returns the hotline to crisis footing."
+chaosx.nr23.163.a: "Suspend our release orders."
+chaosx.nr23.163.b: "Refuse the offer."
+chaosx.nr23.170.t: "Review of the Broken Chain"
+chaosx.nr23.170.d: "The Soviet command chain has been damaged around a registered nuclear depot. The review separates what remains in Soviet hands from what is physically held by a successor authority, what can be recovered, and what must be marked missing or dismantled."
+chaosx.nr23.170.a: "Open the custody board."
+
+chaosx.news.230.t: "The Soviet Test Site Speaks"
+chaosx.news.230.d: "A Soviet atomic demonstration has made the arsenal visible to the world. The remote blast proves that Soviet delivery crews can release a working weapon, and every major government is reassessing its air defenses and war plans."
+chaosx.news.230.a: "The secret is over."
+chaosx.news.231.t: "Moscow Names Its Demand"
+chaosx.news.231.d: "The Soviet Union has issued a nuclear-backed ultimatum to a selected government. Diplomats are testing whether the demand can be settled without a strike while military staffs prepare for the possibility that it cannot."
+chaosx.news.231.a: "The answer is awaited."
+chaosx.news.232.t: "A Nuclear Strike Is Confirmed"
+chaosx.news.232.d: "A Soviet nuclear device has detonated against its target. Contamination spreads beyond the blast zone as casualty lists grow, foreign governments condemn the strike, and military staffs prepare for the crisis that follows."
+chaosx.news.232.a: "The detonation is confirmed."
+chaosx.news.233.t: "Retaliation Windows Open"
+chaosx.news.233.d: "Nuclear use has entered an active retaliation cycle. Commanders are choosing between a limited response, reserve preservation, an emergency hotline, and a wider exchange as every confirmed detonation deepens contamination, death, and panic."
+chaosx.news.233.a: "Hold the response line."
+chaosx.news.234.t: "A Depot Answers to Another Flag"
+chaosx.news.234.d: "A successor authority holds a registered nuclear depot outside the Soviet command chain. The devices remain physically accounted for. Technical access, command formation, and delivery integration must each be completed before the arsenal can become operational."
+chaosx.news.234.a: "Track the custody transfer."
+
