+chaosx.nr29.1.desc: "Surveyors in [riches_found_mine_state.GetName] have uncovered a deposit rich enough to draw miners, merchants, claimants, and thieves within days. Roads are filling with wagons, and the first camps already spread beyond the marked ground. We must decide who may work the find and who will answer for the settlement growing around it."
+chaosx.nr29.1.desc.evolution_i: "Surveyors in [riches_found_mine_state.GetName] have uncovered a deposit rich enough to redraw the national budget before the first shaft is timbered. Ministries issue overlapping permits, party agents promise jobs, and intermediaries approach local officials while the first shipment is still being weighed. We must decide who may work the find and who will answer for the settlement growing around it."
+chaosx.nr29.1.desc.evolution_ii: "Surveyors in [riches_found_mine_state.GetName] have uncovered a deposit whose first specimens already pass from hand to hidden pocket. Guards search the survey crews, officials refuse to release the assay, and families follow the sample wagons as if ordinary stone carried a private claim upon them. We must decide who may work the find and who will answer for the settlement growing around it."
+chaosx.nr29.1.desc.evolution_iii: "Surveyors in [riches_found_mine_state.GetName] have uncovered a deposit beneath workings absent from every map. Knocks answer the number of people underground, a sealed sample returns after removal, and the first ledger balances against no recorded sale. We must decide who may work the find and who will answer for the settlement growing around it."
+chaosx.nr29.1.a: "Build a public fortune."
+chaosx.nr29.1.a.tt: "Public Development raises Mine Development, Local Order, and Revenue Legitimacy while easing Extraction Pressure."
+chaosx.nr29.1.b: "Make the mine an instrument of state."
+chaosx.nr29.1.b.tt: "State Extraction raises Mine Development and Local Order, but stronger output raises Extraction Pressure and weakens Revenue Legitimacy."
+chaosx.nr29.1.c: "Invite a concession economy."
+chaosx.nr29.1.c.tt: "Foreign capital accelerates Mine Development and raises concession exposure. Extraction Pressure rises while local confidence slips."
+chaosx.nr29.1.d: "Place the mine under armed authority."
+chaosx.nr29.1.d.tt: "A Militarized Mine raises Local Order and readiness, but Extraction Pressure and private security autonomy grow."
+chaosx.nr29.1.e: "Take everything the mountain will yield."
+chaosx.nr29.1.e.tt: "Predatory Extraction drives Mine Development and Extraction Pressure upward while Local Order, Revenue Legitimacy, and public control erode."
 
