 ﻿l_english:
 chaosx.nr33.1.t: "Acid Rain"
+chaosx.nr33.report_close: "Return to the response"
+chaosx.nr33.news_close: "The rain reaches farther"
 
-chaosx.nr33.2.t: "Acid Rain on our territory"
-chaosx.nr33.2.d: "Acid rain is ravaging our land, waterways, and ecosystems. The cause remains unknown. Trees wither, aquatic habitats collapse, and crops fail under the acidic downpour. Thousands of people have died."
-chaosx.nr33.2.a: "Take cover!"
+chaosx.nr33.101.t: "The Rain Reaches [acid_rain_report_state.GetName]"
+chaosx.nr33.101.d: "Corrosive rain has entered [acid_rain_report_state.GetName]. Exposed water, crops, roads, and rail equipment are deteriorating, and people caught outside risk burns and respiratory injury. National Preparedness stands at §Y[?acid_rain_preparedness|1]§!. Emergency measures are available for the states under the cloud."
+chaosx.nr33.102.t: "Acid Rain Approaches"
+chaosx.nr33.102.d: "The moving front is expected to reach our controlled territory after its current regional passage. The exact footprint remains uncertain. Civil-defense offices have opened shelters, reservoir crews are covering intakes, and transport authorities are moving exposed equipment while there is still time."
+chaosx.nr33.103.t: "A Severe Cell Forms over [acid_rain_report_state.GetName]"
+chaosx.nr33.103.d: "A concentrated cell will strike [acid_rain_report_state.GetName] after a three-day forecast. Evacuation must finish before the first severe pulse to provide full protection, though one complete day of movement provides a partial benefit."
+chaosx.nr33.104.t: "The Severe Rain Falls"
+chaosx.nr33.104.d: "The first severe pulse has crossed [acid_rain_report_state.GetName]. The ledger records §R[?acid_rain_event_deaths|0]§! cumulative national deaths and an estimated §G[?acid_rain_prevented_deaths|0]§! deaths prevented. Shelter, evacuation, and medical preparations determine how much of the remaining episode the population can endure."
+chaosx.nr33.105.t: "The National Toll Rises"
+chaosx.nr33.105.d: "The Acid Rain ledger records §R[?acid_rain_event_deaths|0]§! deaths in our territory. §Y[?acid_rain_active_exposed_states|0]§! controlled states remain exposed, and Preparedness stands at §Y[?acid_rain_preparedness|1]§!. Shelter, water, medical, and transport weaknesses will shape each later pulse."
+chaosx.nr33.106.t: "Preparation Saves Lives"
+chaosx.nr33.106.d: "Shelters, protected supplies, medical teams, and evacuation work have prevented an estimated §G[?acid_rain_prevented_deaths|0]§! deaths. The estimate compares the recorded outcome with the same exposure without those protections. It does not claim certainty about any individual life."
+chaosx.nr33.107.t: "The Front Leaves Our Territory"
+chaosx.nr33.107.d: "No controlled state remains under acute Acid Rain. The national ledger records §R[?acid_rain_event_deaths|0]§! deaths and an estimated §G[?acid_rain_prevented_deaths|0]§! deaths prevented. Corrosion and contaminated runoff remain in states that have not completed recovery."
+chaosx.nr33.108.t: "Severe Storm Cells"
+chaosx.nr33.108.d: "Concentrated cells are forming inside the broader rain front. Their short forecasts mark several states for heavier corrosion, supply disruption, and lethal exposure. Shelters, medical capacity, and early evacuation can reduce the losses after a cell forms."
+chaosx.nr33.109.t: "The Acute Rain Ends"
+chaosx.nr33.109.d: "The corrosive clouds have dispersed, but damaged railways, poisoned runoff, and stripped machinery remain. National recovery will continue until every affected state is repaired or decontaminated and all temporary commitments are closed."
+chaosx.nr33.110.t: "Recovery Work Completed in [acid_rain_report_state.GetName]"
+chaosx.nr33.110.d: "Crews in [acid_rain_report_state.GetName] have completed the selected recovery operation. Transport repairs, decontamination, or industrial work have reduced the state's recorded aftermath without restoring more damage than the rain caused."
+chaosx.nr33.111.t: "A Global Acid Layer Forms"
+chaosx.nr33.111.d: "The regional fronts are merging into one atmospheric layer. In three days, corrosive rain will reach every valid inhabited state at once. Existing preparations remain effective, and countries can still complete urgent work before later pulses."
+chaosx.nr33.112.t: "Global Acid Rain"
+chaosx.nr33.112.d: "Corrosive rain now covers every valid inhabited state. Regional superstorms can form inside the global layer, each giving its threatened states three days of warning. The layer will persist for at least forty-five days before its first dissipation check can succeed."
+chaosx.nr33.113.t: "The Front Divides"
+chaosx.nr33.113.d: "The atmospheric mass is separating into independent weather fronts. A second front will stabilize in seven days and begin its own regional passage, warnings, intensity changes, and severe-cell cycle."
+chaosx.nr33.114.t: "The Rain Concentrates"
+chaosx.nr33.114.d: "In three days, the strongest parts of the moving front may begin producing severe storm cells. Each cell will identify its threatened states before impact, leaving a short interval for shelter work, medical preparation, and evacuation."
 
-chaosx.news.37.t: "Acid Rain"
-chaosx.news.37.d: "Acid rain is sweeping across continents and eroding infrastructure, contaminating water, and killing crops. Industrial emissions and deforestation may be feeding the corrosive clouds, and governments are searching for a way to stop them."
-chaosx.news.37.a: "The damage is severe."
+chaosx.nr33.201.t: "Acid Rain Forms"
+chaosx.nr33.201.d: "A lethal corrosive rain system has formed and begun moving between regions. Water supplies, crops, roads, railways, and exposed machinery lie in its path. Governments are opening civil-defense stores and preparing for a cloud whose origin remains unknown."
+chaosx.nr33.202.t: "A Second Acid-Rain Front"
+chaosx.nr33.202.d: "The corrosive weather has divided into two stable fronts. Each mass now moves independently, carrying its own warnings and severe cells into regions that may have believed the danger had passed."
+chaosx.nr33.203.t: "A Third Front Stabilizes"
+chaosx.nr33.203.d: "A third acid-rain front has stabilized. Separate cloud systems now cross the world on their own schedules, widening the territory exposed to poisoned runoff, corrosion, and respiratory injury."
+chaosx.nr33.204.t: "Acid Rain Covers the World"
+chaosx.nr33.204.d: "The fronts have merged into a global atmospheric layer. Corrosive rain is falling across every valid inhabited state, and concentrated superstorms are forming inside the wider cloud."
+chaosx.nr33.205.t: "The Corrosive Clouds Disperse"
+chaosx.nr33.205.d: "The last acute Acid Rain has stopped. Corroded infrastructure and contaminated water remain across the states it touched, and national recovery work will continue after the clouds disperse."
 
-chaosx.news.38.t: "Acid clouds disappear!"
-chaosx.news.38.d: "The ominous clouds that had shrouded the skies for weeks have suddenly vanished, bringing a sense of relief and optimism to communities worldwide. With the disappearance of the oppressive cloud cover, sunlight streams through once more, restoring a sense of normalcy and hope to people's lives. As the gloom lifts, activities resume, and spirits soar, signaling a newfound resilience in the face of adversity. With brighter days ahead, communities unite in gratitude and determination to rebuild and move forward."
-chaosx.news.38.a: "The skies are clear again."
+chaosx_acid_rain_decision_category: "Acid Rain Response"
+chaosx_acid_rain_decision_category_desc: "Moving fronts expose states to lethal rain, corrosion, supply disruption, and contaminated runoff. Permanent projects raise national Preparedness. Urgent actions protect people during warnings and exposure, while recovery actions repair the aftermath. Equipment and fuel are consumed. Reserved manpower returns once, and committed civilian factories are released once when the work completes or closes safely."
+chaosx_acid_rain_project_shelter: "Expand the Shelter Network"
+chaosx_acid_rain_project_shelter_desc: "Raise the Shelter Network by one tier, up to tier 4. Each completed tier adds §G7.5 Preparedness§! and improves protection from opening shocks and severe cells. Support equipment is consumed. Manpower is reserved and civilian factories remain committed until completion or safe cancellation."
+chaosx_acid_rain_project_water: "Protect Water and Food"
+chaosx_acid_rain_project_water_desc: "Raise Protected Water and Food by one tier, up to tier 4. Each completed tier adds §G6.25 Preparedness§!, reduces sustained losses, and limits contaminated runoff and aftermath. The quoted route consumes trains for land supply or convoys for island and overseas supply, never both."
+chaosx_acid_rain_project_medical: "Expand Medical and Protective Capacity"
+chaosx_acid_rain_project_medical_desc: "Raise Medical and Protective Capacity by one tier, up to tier 4. Each completed tier adds §G6.25 Preparedness§!, reduces sustained and severe-cell losses, and improves recovery. Support equipment and fuel are consumed. Manpower is reserved until the work closes."
+chaosx_acid_rain_project_transport: "Harden Transport and Infrastructure"
+chaosx_acid_rain_project_transport_desc: "Raise Transport and Infrastructure Resilience by one tier, up to tier 4. Each completed tier adds §G5 Preparedness§!, reduces building-damage pressure, strengthens evacuation, and limits acute supply and movement disruption. Trains, trucks, and fuel are consumed."
+
+chaosx_acid_rain_urgent_shelter: "Activate Shelter Protocols"
+chaosx_acid_rain_urgent_shelter_desc: "A fourteen-day national action that reduces opening and sustained losses for twenty-one days or until exposure ends. Shelter tiers strengthen the result. Political power and support equipment are spent, while manpower is reserved until the commitment closes."
+chaosx_acid_rain_urgent_water: "Secure Emergency Water and Food"
+chaosx_acid_rain_urgent_water_desc: "A twenty-one-day national action that reduces sustained losses and aftermath growth for thirty days. The land route consumes trains, while the island and overseas route consumes convoys. Both routes consume support equipment and reserve manpower."
+chaosx_acid_rain_urgent_medical: "Open an Emergency Medical Surge"
+chaosx_acid_rain_urgent_medical_desc: "A fourteen-day national action that reduces sustained losses and severe-cell casualty pressure for twenty-one days. Support equipment and fuel are consumed, manpower is reserved, and medical fatigue follows the operation."
+chaosx_acid_rain_urgent_transport: "Reroute Transport and Repair Crews"
+chaosx_acid_rain_urgent_transport_desc: "A fourteen-day national action that limits acute supply disruption and building-damage pressure for twenty-one days. It consumes the quoted trains, trucks, and fuel and requires a valid transport stockpile."
+chaosx_acid_rain_urgent_evacuate: "Evacuate [FROM.GetName]"
+chaosx_acid_rain_urgent_evacuate_desc: "Move civilians under a severe-cell or superstorm forecast. One complete day provides partial protection, and completion before the first severe pulse provides the full benefit. The action lasts seven days and consumes the quoted transport and fuel while reserving manpower. Production, construction, and supply efficiency fall temporarily in [FROM.GetName]."
+
+chaosx_acid_rain_recovery_transport: "Restore Transport in [FROM.GetName]"
+chaosx_acid_rain_recovery_transport_desc: "Commit crews for twenty-eight days to repair railways and infrastructure in [FROM.GetName]. The work consumes trains, trucks, and fuel, commits one civilian factory, reduces transport aftermath, and repairs only damage recorded from the rain."
+chaosx_acid_rain_recovery_decontaminate: "Decontaminate [FROM.GetName]"
+chaosx_acid_rain_recovery_decontaminate_desc: "Commit crews for thirty-five days to clean water and soil in [FROM.GetName]. The work consumes support equipment and either trains or convoys, reserves manpower, commits one civilian factory, and lowers environmental aftermath and contaminated-water pressure."
+chaosx_acid_rain_recovery_industry: "Repair Industry in [FROM.GetName]"
+chaosx_acid_rain_recovery_industry_desc: "Commit crews for thirty-five days to repair exposed industry in [FROM.GetName]. The work consumes support equipment, reserves manpower, commits one civilian factory, and cannot restore more factory levels than the rain damaged."
+chaosx_acid_rain_recovery_demobilize: "Demobilize the Emergency Apparatus"
+chaosx_acid_rain_recovery_demobilize_desc: "Spend seven days closing the emergency organization after national exposure has ended. Valid manpower reserves return, civilian commitments close, and medical fatigue is cleared. Consumed equipment, fuel, trains, convoys, trucks, and political power are not refunded."
+
