diff --git a/localisation/english/chaosx_gui_l_english.yml b/localisation/english/chaosx_gui_l_english.yml
index 786d4abcab..171c5a2e1f 100644
--- a/localisation/english/chaosx_gui_l_english.yml
+++ b/localisation/english/chaosx_gui_l_english.yml
@@ -53,7 +53,7 @@ chaosx.help.tab.chaos_meter: "Chaos"
 chaosx.help.tab.warfare: "Warfare"
 chaosx.help.tab.controls: "Controls"
 chaosx.help.body.overview: "§YCurrent State§!\nChaos: [GetChaosMeterValueColored]  Tier: §Y[GetChaosTierName]§!\nCurrent timer: §Y[?event_timer_days|0]§! days  Dynamic timer: §Y[?timer_window_dynamic_min_days|0]§!-§Y[?timer_window_dynamic_max_days|0]§! days\nEvents fired: §Y[?global.total_events_fired|0]§!  Evolutions fired: §Y[?global.events_log_evolution_sequence|0]§!\nClusters fired: §Y[?global.total_event_clusters_fired|0]§!\n\n§YCore Loop§!\nChaos Redux uses one global Chaos Meter and a weighted event pool. Each eligible player country has its own timer. When a timer reaches zero, the system checks which events are valid, skips disabled or already-spent events, and then picks from the remaining weights. The dynamic timer is the effective roll range after timer caps, day reductions, and the current chaos modifier are applied.\n\n§YPlayer Control§!\nSettings let you pause automatic events for your country, trigger events or clusters by hand, adjust timer ranges, tune weights and recovery, and inspect history. Event Logs show what fired, what is still available, and which staged systems have advanced.\n\n§YMultiplayer§!\nMultiplayer uses the same global event pool and Chaos Meter for everyone, so major world state stays shared. Player countries keep their own timers and event-system toggles, so one player can pause automatic events without stopping the whole campaign. Global systems such as deaths, air contamination, famine, migration, camp repression, scenarios, super-events, and world-end consequences can affect the shared world."
-chaosx.help.body.events: "§YLive Values§!\nEvents fired: §Y[?global.total_events_fired|0]§!  Unique events left: §Y[?global.unfired_total_events_count|0]§!\nMajor left: §Y[?global.unfired_major_events_count|0]§!  Fire once left: §Y[?global.unfired_fire_once_events_count|0]§!  Repeatable never fired: §Y[?global.unfired_repeatable_events_count|0]§!\nDisabled events: §Y[?global.disabled_events^num|0]§!\n\n§YEvent Types§!\nRepeatable events can return to the automatic pool after firing, so they may appear several times when their triggers and recovered weight allow it. Fire once events are ordinary unique events. After they fire automatically, they leave the normal pool. Major events are unique high-impact events with their own count and gating. After firing, they also leave normal automatic selection unless fired manually.\n\n§YEvolutions§!\nEvolutions are staged progress markers inside a larger event system, not separate event rolls. When a stage fires, the log records how far that system has advanced.\n\n§YClusters§!\nFixed-member clusters begin with an eligible trigger, guarantee required members, and roll optional members by severity and current Chaos. They may add stricter gates but can never override event-system fireability. Random Stuff is different: after an ordinary automatic minor event, it can draw 3 to 5 events uniformly from the entire currently fireable pool.\n\n§YWorld-End Scenarios§!\nWorld-end scenarios are terminal branches unlocked at World Collapse tier. An enabled branch can resolve the campaign from the global situation, and once an end state is active, automatic event firing is disabled for all countries."
+chaosx.help.body.events: "§YLive Values§!\nEvents fired: §Y[?global.total_events_fired|0]§!  Unique events left: §Y[?global.unfired_total_events_count|0]§!\nMajor left: §Y[?global.unfired_major_events_count|0]§!  Fire once left: §Y[?global.unfired_fire_once_events_count|0]§!  Repeatable never fired: §Y[?global.unfired_repeatable_events_count|0]§!\nDisabled events: §Y[?global.disabled_events^num|0]§!\n\n§YEvent Types§!\nRepeatable events can return to the automatic pool after firing, so they may appear several times when their triggers and recovered weight allow it. Fire once events are ordinary unique events. After they fire automatically, they leave the normal pool. Major events are unique high-impact events with their own count and gating. After firing, they also leave normal automatic selection unless fired manually.\n\n§YEvolutions§!\nEvolutions are staged progress markers inside a larger event system, not separate event rolls. When a stage fires, the log records how far that system has advanced.\n\n§YClusters§!\nFixed-member clusters begin with an eligible trigger, guarantee required members, and roll optional members by severity and current Chaos. They may add stricter gates but can never override event-system fireability. Random Stuff is different: after an ordinary automatic minor event, it can draw 3 to 5 events uniformly from the entire currently fireable pool.\n\n§YWorld-End Scenarios§!\nWorld-end scenarios are world-ending outcomes unlocked at World Collapse tier. An enabled outcome can resolve the campaign from the global situation, and once one begins, automatic event firing is disabled for all countries."
 chaosx.help.body.chaos_meter: "§YLive Values§!\nChaos: [GetChaosMeterValueColored]  Tier: §Y[GetChaosTierName]§!\nTimer modifier: §Y[?global.chaos_timer_modifier|.2]x§!\nRecorded deaths: §Y[GetChaosMeterDeathsTotalDisplay]§!\nAir contamination: [GetAirContaminationValueColored]\n\n§YChaos Meter§!\nThe global Chaos Meter shortens event timing, unlocks stronger escalation, and increases eligible cluster pressure as its tier rises.\n\n§YDeaths System§!\nMilitary casualties and state-linked civilian deaths from war, disasters, disease, famine, forced displacement, camps, and unconventional weapons enter one shared ledger. Civilian entries remove real state population, and each source can convert its recorded toll into chaos.\n\n§YAir Cleanliness§!\nAir Cleanliness tracks atmospheric contamination from chemical hazards, outbreaks, fallout, smoke, ash, and aerosols. Thresholds at 25%, 50%, 75%, and 100% accelerate outbreaks, worsen Air Winter, activate the Air Cleanliness Treaty, and can enable the Fallout consequence. Its Chaos Meter tab shows recovery and a permanent source ledger.\n\n§YFamine Mechanics§!\nFamine tracks Food Security, Food Reserves, and Relief Access in each affected state. Conditions progress through stable, supply strain, acute shortage, famine, and catastrophic famine. Relief, route, reserve, import, airlift, and evacuation actions can reverse pressure, while severe mortality enters the Deaths System and may create a separate migration request.\n\n§YMigration Mechanics§!\nMigration tracks Displacement Load, Reception Capacity, and Border Policy as cohorts move through flight, reception, settlement, resettlement, and return. Population moves between proven origins and destinations; unsafe routes or violent pushback can add deaths. Decisions, missions, reports, and the migration mapmode manage corridors and outcomes.\n\n§YCamp System Mechanics§!\nThe Repression and Camps System covers detention, forced labor, gulags, experiment programs, discovery, reform, and dismantlement. Active sites remove real population through the Deaths System and store responsibility and evidence for later Condemnation. Country routes and its five tabs show territories, active sites, programs, discovery, and reform without revealing hidden evidence early."
 chaosx.help.body.warfare: "§YChaos Warfare§!\nChaos warfare covers weapons and military systems that change a war beyond normal battles. These systems are meant to create lasting territory problems as well as battlefield effects.\n\n§YChemical Warfare§!\nChemical warfare is built around agents, delivery methods, protective gear, and contamination. It can use shells, projectors, aircraft, or other delivery paths, and it can leave chemical contamination in states. Chemical pressure can affect combat, state safety, cleanup needs, diplomatic reaction, and long-term chaos.\n\n§YBiological Warfare§!\nBiological warfare is built around research projects, facilities, pathogens, defenses, field tests, and outbreak control. Biological attacks can create disease contamination or outbreaks, force prevention and cure decisions, and leave long-term hazards in affected states. The main danger is that effects can keep spreading after the original attack.\n\n§YContamination And Mitigation§!\nChemical, biological, and nuclear contamination are tracked at state level. Cleanup, filters, masks, medical defenses, doctrine, technologies, and decisions change duration, strength, and exposure. The mapmode helps find contaminated states, while death and chaos systems record severe failures."
 chaosx.help.body.controls: "§YShortcuts§!\nSettings: §YCtrl+Shift+C§!\nChaos Meter: §YCtrl+Shift+M§!\nEvent Logs toggle: §YCtrl+Shift+E§!\nEvent Logs Events tab: §YCtrl+E§!\nEvent Timer: §YCtrl+Shift+T§!\nScenarios: §YCtrl+Shift+S§!\nHelp: §YCtrl+Shift+H§!\nDisable Event System toggle: §YCtrl+Shift+D§!\n\n§YSettings§!\nTrigger Events lets you select, filter, and manually fire event IDs or event clusters. Timer System controls the automatic event interval and tag eligibility. Chaos Meter controls the global chaos value and world-end settings. Advanced Settings tunes event weights, recovery, repeatable cap behavior, and timing. Miscellaneous contains utility and super-event audio controls. Scenarios opens manual sandbox and challenge setups.\n\n§YEvent Log Windows§!\nRows in History, Events, Evolutions, and Clusters open detail windows. Event, evolution, and cluster detail windows are movable and can be used for inspection or manual triggering."
