 chaosx.events_log.window.event_details.communism_spread: "Communist organizers turn propaganda networks and local agitation into control of vulnerable states. As their foothold deepens, agitation can harden into insurgent strongholds and lockdowns, raising the risk of revolt.\n\nGovernments can intervene locally or launch a broader emergency response. Delay gives the movement more chances to spread, stage unexpected uprisings, and draw the country toward revolution."
 chaosx.events_log.window.event_details.zombie_outbreak: "A zombie outbreak erupts in a populous state and grows by consuming the people and territory in its path. Crowded, underdeveloped regions face the greatest risk of secondary outbreaks, while each evolution makes the horde harder to contain.\n\nCountries can fortify the front, reduce outbreak risk, pursue a cure, and coordinate through the Anti-Zombie League. If the horde gains momentum, it can spread faster than isolated governments can respond."
 chaosx.events_log.window.event_details.random_war: "Random War turns border orders, panicked ultimatums, and opportunistic claims into sudden declarations between eligible sovereign countries.\n\nHigher chaos tiers unlock War Contagion stages that spread one incident into a wider war web. Later stages can draw compatible Chaos Redux special countries, major powers, and faction members into the chain."
-chaosx.events_log.window.event_details.soviet_collapse: "The Soviet Union is losing command over its republics, rail offices, garrisons, and depots. Moscow can answer with force, negotiation, isolation, or party discipline, but each visible failure gives local authorities more room to act.\n\nCurrent reading: [GetEventsLogSovietCollapseDetailCrisisState]\nFirst wave: [GetEventsLogSovietCollapseDetailFirstWave]\nFree Republics' League: [GetEventsLogSovietCollapseDetailLeague]\nMoscow Authority: [GetEventsLogSovietCollapseDetailAuthority]\nUnion Crisis Threat: [GetEventsLogSovietCollapseDetailThreat]\nForeign intervention: [GetEventsLogSovietCollapseDetailForeign]\nOld movements and splinters: [GetEventsLogSovietCollapseDetailMutation]\n\nForced-labor quotas, grain extraction, and NKVD campaigns can briefly reinforce Moscow's authority, but each use deepens famine pressure, republic fear, old-movement grievance, and the evidence record. Once the crisis becomes severe, repression can no longer reduce the terminal threat.\n\nBreakaway republics can seek recognition, seize depots, coordinate defenses, or draw more republics into the crisis while Moscow tries to restore command or force a new settlement."
+chaosx.events_log.window.event_details.soviet_collapse: "The Soviet Union is losing command over its republics, rail offices, garrisons, and depots. Moscow can answer with force, negotiation, isolation, or party discipline, but each visible failure gives local authorities more room to act.\n\nCurrent reading: [GetEventsLogSovietCollapseDetailCrisisState]\nFirst wave: [GetEventsLogSovietCollapseDetailFirstWave]\nFree Republics' League: [GetEventsLogSovietCollapseDetailLeague]\nMoscow Authority: [GetEventsLogSovietCollapseDetailAuthority]\nUnion Crisis Threat: [GetEventsLogSovietCollapseDetailThreat]\nForeign intervention: [GetEventsLogSovietCollapseDetailForeign]\nOld movements and splinters: [GetEventsLogSovietCollapseDetailMutation]\n\nForced-labor quotas, grain extraction, and NKVD campaigns can briefly reinforce Moscow's authority, but each use deepens famine pressure, republic fear, old-movement grievance, and the record of atrocities. Once the crisis becomes severe, repression can no longer prevent an irreversible rupture of the Union.\n\nBreakaway republics can seek recognition, seize depots, coordinate defenses, or draw more republics into the crisis while Moscow tries to restore command or force a new settlement."
 chaosx.events_log.window.event_details.fury: "An unnatural rage seizes a minor country and turns it into a rogue war state. Fury columns gather supplies and reinforcements, then attack neighboring countries as conquest feeds the violence.\n\nThe crisis can harden the first Fury state, ignite rival or allied outbreaks, and end in simultaneous wars across every available border."
 chaosx.events_log.window.event_details.white_peace: "Exhausted belligerents accept peace without conquest or indemnity, restoring the borders they held before the war. Early settlements close a single war between minor countries.\n\nAs the event evolves, several minor wars can end together, major powers may rarely be included, and a wider diplomatic settlement can quiet a world crowded with wars."
 chaosx.events_log.window.event_details.death.pre_reveal: "Death first appears through missing island traffic. Mail boats fail to return, radio rooms stop answering, and port offices cannot confirm any arrivals from the affected island.\n\nAt this stage there is no public enemy. A country that receives the report can ignore it, restrict sea traffic, preserve the records, or send a survey boat while the problem is still small."
