 chaosx.fallout.68.t: "The Capital Report Returns"
 chaosx.fallout.68.seal.success.d: "The sealed civic core in the assigned capital held through the coldest shifts. Filters were replaced before the next ash fall, fuel crews kept the public rooms warm, and one damaged infrastructure level was brought back into service. Exposure fell by the recorded amount while shelter and recovery improved under the [This.GetFalloutOrientationArchetypeName] administration."
 chaosx.fallout.68.seal.partial.d: "The civic core remained usable, although fuel crews could not heat every public room and the repair schedule reached only its first section. Exposure fell by the partial amount and the [This.GetFalloutOrientationArchetypeName] retains a capital that still depends on district deliveries."
@@ -6390,14 +6390,14 @@ chaosx.fallout.68.seal.failure.d: "The civic sealing order failed in the assigne
 chaosx.fallout.68.disperse.success.d: "Stores and offices now work from a chain of district rooms rather than one exposed civic center. The move gave the [This.GetFalloutOrientationArchetypeName] more shelter, stronger adaptation, and a reliable route for supplies even while the capital's old offices remain dark."
 chaosx.fallout.68.disperse.partial.d: "The distribution plan reached the largest surviving districts, but several offices kept private store books and the route schedule remains uneven. Shelter and adaptation improved by the partial amount while supply access gained only the value that the damaged roads could carry."
 chaosx.fallout.68.disperse.failure.d: "The attempted dispersal scattered stores without creating a working office network. Shelter claims multiplied, supply access fell, and the [This.GetFalloutOrientationArchetypeName] must answer for food and power consumed by empty transfer rooms. The Deaths ledger remains closed because the failure was recorded as a logistics loss rather than an unreported disappearance."
-chaosx.fallout.68.evacuate.success.d: "The prepared receiving state accepted the full migration request from the poisoned capital. Source population fell by the exact number transferred, the destination ledger received the same people and its shelter gain, and no person was created or lost outside the balanced Deaths receipt."
+chaosx.fallout.68.evacuate.success.d: "The prepared receiving state accepted the full migration request from the poisoned capital. The same number of people who left the source arrived at the destination, where the expanded shelters received them. Every evacuee is accounted for."
 chaosx.fallout.68.evacuate.partial.d: "The receiving shelters accepted only part of the planned movement before their doors reached capacity. The source and destination ledgers match the reduced request, exposure fell by the partial amount, and the [This.GetFalloutOrientationArchetypeName] must keep the remaining capital wards under a tighter watch."
-chaosx.fallout.68.evacuate.failure.d: "The evacuation convoy broke apart between the poisoned core and the prepared receiving state. A smaller movement still left the source ledger, the destination ledger, and the Deaths receipt balanced, but exposure rose and the capital now carries the memory of a failed departure."
+chaosx.fallout.68.evacuate.failure.d: "The evacuation convoy broke apart between the poisoned core and the prepared receiving state. A smaller group still reached the destination, but others died along the route. Exposure rose, and the capital now carries the memory of a failed departure."
